// A call-form name present in both namespaces [F9]: the struct and the
// function share `page`; the call is an ambiguity error, never a
// priority search. A tag beside the fn coexists since F9.5 — the call
// form always means the fn — so the residual class is the constructor
// declaration. The brace form and the bare use still resolve (their own
// positions), so only the call reports.

tag int
struct page { n: int }
fn page(n: int) -> int { n }
fn caller(n: int) -> int { page(n) }
